-- every continuation a CPS function is given is called with the memory base (or a value it
-- loaded), and every continuation uses what it is given: a closure whose body did not use its own
-- variable would be lifted out of it and evaluated before the step it is to follow
-- the base, given back through a value just computed, so that what follows depends on it
hv2-keep : Word → Word → Word
hv2-keep m r = %wsub (%wadd m r) r
